    <bpmn:process id="W_W1036" name="W1036. Customer Digital Product Passport &amp; Sustainability Information Access" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer scans product QR code in-store or accesses product sustainability information on buildright.com.ph
Frequency: ~20,000–30,000 scans/month chain-wide; growing with sustainability awareness
Volume: 1 scan per customer interaction; ~35,000 SKUs with digital passports
Owner: Category Manager (content); ESG Officer (compliance)
Participants: Customer, Product Content Manager, Vendor, ESG Data Analyst, Marketing Coordinator
Source: workflow W1036 — Customer Digital Product Passport &amp; Sustainability Information Access</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1036_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1036_Lane1" name="Product Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1036_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1036_Lane3" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1036_Lane4" name="ESG Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1036_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1036_Start6" name="Customer scans product QR code in-store or accesses product sustainability information on…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1036_Task7" name="Digital Product Passport Content Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Digital Product Passport Content Creation: For each SKU (prioritized by category — lumber, paint, electrical, plumbing, insulation first): (a) Product Content Manager collects sustainability data from vendor: (i) environmental certifications (FSC, PEFC, GREENGUARD, ISO 14001, DENR AO compliance), (ii) carbon footprint per unit (from vendor LCA — Life Cycle Assessment, or estimated per ESG data per W694), (iii) material composition (recycled content %, locally sourced %), (iv) chemical safety (VOC level, lead-free, formaldehyde-free), (v) energy/water efficiency ratings (DOE Energy Label, Watersense), (vi) end-of-life guidance (recyclable, biodegradable, proper disposal method per W193), (vii) manufacturer sustainability practices (renewable energy use, waste reduction programs, fair labor practices); (b) Product Content Manager creates DPP content card per SKU in PIM system per W316 (Digital Asset Master); (c) ESG Data Analyst validates data accuracy against vendor certifications and third-party databases; (d) system generates unique QR code per SKU linked to DPP content card
Responsible (R): Product Content Manager / ESG Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per SKU (initial creation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1036_Task8" name="QR Code Integration &amp; In-Store Display">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: QR Code Integration &amp; In-Store Display: (a) DPP QR code integrated into shelf label design per W181 (Store-Level Price Tag Printing): QR code printed in bottom-right corner of every shelf label for DPP-enabled SKUs; (b) QR code also displayed on: (i) buildright.com.ph product page, (ii) BuildRight mobile app product detail screen, (iii) POS receipt for purchased items (link to DPP for post-purchase reference); (c) standard shelf label printers (already deployed at stores per W181) support QR code printing — no hardware change required; (d) Store Staff apply DPP-enabled shelf labels during regular price tag updates per W181
Responsible (R): System / Store Staff
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Integrated into existing W181 process</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1036_Task9" name="Customer Scan &amp; Information Access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer Scan &amp; Information Access: Customer scans QR code with smartphone camera: (a) QR code directs to BuildRight DPP web page optimized for mobile: (i) product name, image, and specifications, (ii) environmental certifications with certification logo and verification link, (iii) carbon footprint displayed as &quot;kg CO₂ per unit&quot; with comparison to category average, (iv) material sustainability score (BuildRight proprietary rating: 1–5 green leaves based on recycled content, local sourcing, and toxicity), (v) end-of-life disposal guidance (&quot;Recyclable: take to BuildRight store for recycling per W157&quot; or &quot;Biodegradable&quot; or &quot;Dispose per municipal waste guidelines&quot;), (vi) link to SDS per W1019 if product is hazardous, (vii) link to full product page on buildright.com.ph for purchase; (b) system tracks scan data: SKU, store location (from QR code), scan timestamp, customer loyalty ID (if logged in)
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: &lt; 5 sec (scan to display)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1036_Task10" name="DPP Content Maintenance &amp; Vendor Data Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DPP Content Maintenance &amp; Vendor Data Update: (a) quarterly: Product Content Manager reviews DPP content for accuracy — certifications expire, vendors change formulations, new certifications obtained; (b) vendor portal (W868) allows vendors to self-update sustainability data with documentation upload; (c) ESG Data Analyst audits vendor-submitted updates: verify certification validity, cross-reference with third-party databases (FSC, GREENGUARD, DOE), flag discrepancies; (d) for vendors unable to provide sustainability data: DPP shows &quot;Sustainability data not yet available for this product. Contact manufacturer directly.&quot; — this creates market pressure on vendors to participate; (e) annual: comprehensive DPP audit coinciding with ESG report preparation per W694
Responsible (R): Product Content Manager / ESG Data Analyst
Accountable (A): ESG Officer
Duration: 2–4 hours/week (ongoing) + 8–12 hours/quarter (audit)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1036_Task11" name="DPP Analytics &amp; Sustainability Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DPP Analytics &amp; Sustainability Reporting: (a) system tracks DPP engagement metrics: scan volume by SKU, by store, by customer segment (B2C vs. trade); (b) scan data feeds ESG reporting per W694: &quot;X% of product catalog has digital product passports; Y customer scans/month accessing sustainability information&quot;; (c) scan data informs merchandising: SKUs with high DPP scan rates indicate customer sustainability interest — consider expanding sustainable alternatives in those categories per W195 (Sustainable Sourcing); (d) marketing uses DPP scan data for targeted campaigns: &quot;You scanned [Product X] — here are similar products with higher sustainability ratings&quot; per W676 (Digital Marketing Campaign Operations)
Responsible (R): ESG Data Analyst / Marketing Coordinator
Accountable (A): ESG Officer
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1036_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1036_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1036_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1036_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Category Manager (content); ESG Officer (compliance) review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (content); ESG Officer (compliance)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1036_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1036_Annotation13" targetRef="W1036_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow15" sourceRef="W1036_Start6" targetRef="W1036_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow16" sourceRef="W1036_Task7" targetRef="W1036_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow17" sourceRef="W1036_Task8" targetRef="W1036_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow18" sourceRef="W1036_Task9" targetRef="W1036_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow19" sourceRef="W1036_Task10" targetRef="W1036_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1036_Flow20" sourceRef="W1036_Task11" targetRef="W1036_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
