    <bpmn:process id="W_W1120" name="W1120. Customer Loyalty Points Donation to Charity / Community Cause" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Loyalty member initiates points donation via mobile app, website, or in-store; or BuildRight activates a corporate cause campaign
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 points donation transactions/month (estimated 1–2% of loyalty members participate)
Volume: 1 cause selection per donation; points transferred in real-time
Owner: Marketing Manager (Loyalty Program)
Participants: Customer (Loyalty Member), Marketing Manager, Finance (GL), Partner Charity/NGO
Source: workflow W1120 — Customer Loyalty Points Donation to Charity / Community Cause</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1120_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1120_Lane1" name="Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1120_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1120_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1120_Lane4" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1120_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1120_Start6" name="Loyalty member initiates points donation via mobile app, website, or in-store; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1120_Task7" name="Charity Partner Onboarding &amp; Cause Campaign Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Charity Partner Onboarding &amp; Cause Campaign Setup: (a) Marketing Manager selects partner charities/NGOs: (i) verified Philippine-registered organizations (SEC-registered, with BIR Certificate of Registration and permit to solicit donations); (ii) causes aligned with BuildRight&#x27;s CSR focus: housing/home building (Gawad Kalinga, Habitat for Humanity Philippines), disaster relief (Philippine Red Cross), community development, education; (iii) maximum 5 active partner causes at any time to avoid choice paralysis; (b) system creates cause profiles in loyalty module: name, description, photo/story, fundraising goal (optional), and fund utilization description; (c) cause campaign activated: (i) always-available general donation option; (ii) time-limited campaigns (e.g., &quot;Typhoon Odette Rebuild Fund — Donate points through December 31&quot;); (iii) BuildRight match commitment announced (e.g., &quot;BuildRight will match 50% of all points donated this month&quot;)
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–4 hours per campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1120_Task8" name="Member Points Donation Action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Member Points Donation Action: (a) loyalty member donates points via: (i) mobile app: &quot;Donate Points&quot; feature on loyalty dashboard — select cause, enter points amount (minimum 10 points), confirm; (ii) website: same flow on web loyalty portal; (iii) in-store at POS: cashier enters donation during checkout — &quot;Would you like to donate your points to [Current Cause]?&quot; (optional prompt, not aggressive); (iv) SMS: text &quot;DONATE [points] [cause code]&quot; to BuildRight short code; (b) system processes donation: (i) validates member has sufficient points balance; (ii) deducts points from member account immediately; (iii) adds points to cause&#x27;s running total (visible to all members); (iv) sends confirmation SMS/email: &quot;You donated [X] points to [Cause]. Thank you for making a difference!&quot;; (v) awards a &quot;Community Champion&quot; loyalty badge to the member&#x27;s profile (gamification); (vi) member receives an acknowledgment receipt via email (points donations are not tax-deductible for the member — only BuildRight&#x27;s corporate match is deductible, per the pain points)
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 1–2 min (customer self-service)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1120_Task9" name="Corporate Match Calculation &amp; Liability Release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Corporate Match Calculation &amp; Liability Release: (a) at end of each month, system calculates: (i) total member points donated per cause; (ii) BuildRight corporate match (if applicable): e.g., 50% match = BuildRight contributes additional 0.5 points per member point donated; (iii) total cash value = (member points + corporate match) × PHP 1.00/point; (b) accounting entries: (i) debit Loyalty Liability (member points donated — liability released); (ii) debit CSR Expense (corporate match contribution); (iii) credit Cash / Payable to Charity; (c) system generates quarterly disbursement report per charity partner
Responsible (R): System / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: automated monthly; 1–2 hours/quarter for disbursement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1120_Task10" name="Quarterly Charity Disbursement &amp; Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly Charity Disbursement &amp; Reporting: (a) Finance processes quarterly disbursement to partner charities: (i) payment via bank transfer to charity&#x27;s verified bank account; (ii) BIR donation documentation generated for BuildRight&#x27;s tax records; (iii) charity acknowledges receipt and provides fund utilization report; (b) Marketing publishes impact report on website and app: (i) &quot;In Q3 2026, BuildRight customers donated [X] points (PHP [Y]) to [Charity]. This funded [Z] homes / [Z] relief packs / [Z] school rooms.&quot;; (ii) top donating stores recognized; (iii) individual donors who contributed ≥ 10,000 points receive a thank-you email from the charity; (c) impact stories developed for social media (W142) and newsletter
Responsible (R): Finance / Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1120_Task11" name="Program Performance Review &amp; Optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Program Performance Review &amp; Optimization: (a) Marketing Manager reviews program metrics quarterly: (i) participation rate (% of active members who donated); (ii) average points donated per transaction; (iii) total points donated vs. total points expiring (comparison to W570); (iv) cause preference analysis (which causes attract most donations?); (v) seasonal patterns (holiday surge, disaster relief spikes); (vi) member retention correlation (do donors have higher retention?); (b) program adjustments: (i) rotate causes based on preference data; (ii) increase match percentage during low-donation periods; (iii) test new donation prompts (POS, email, SMS); (c) annual program report for CSR committee (W135) and financial governance review (W104)
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1120_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1120_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1120_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1120_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Marketing Manager (Loyalty Program) review and approval gate
Owner: Marketing Manager (Loyalty Program)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1120_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1120_Annotation13" targetRef="W1120_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
