    <bpmn:process id="W_W1186" name="W1186. Loyalty Program Partner Cross-Promotion &amp; Third-Party Reward Integration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Partnership opportunity identified; quarterly partner review; or campaign planning cycle
Frequency: ~3–5 active partnerships at any time; quarterly partner performance review; annual contract renewal
Volume: ~90,000–120,000 loyalty program members engaging with partner offers/month (~15–20% of the ~600K base cross-participate)
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager
Participants: Loyalty Program Manager, Partnership Manager (Marketing), Category Manager, Finance, Legal, Partner Representative
Source: workflow W1186 — Loyalty Program Partner Cross-Promotion &amp; Third-Party Reward Integration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1186_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1186_Lane1" name="Loyalty Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1186_Lane2" name="Partnership Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1186_Lane3" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1186_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1186_Start5" name="Partnership opportunity identified; quarterly partner review; or campaign planning cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task6" name="Partner identification &amp; evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Partner identification &amp; evaluation: (a) Loyalty Program Manager and Partnership Manager identify potential partners based on: (i) audience overlap with BuildRight customers (homeowners, DIYers, contractors), (ii) brand alignment and reputation, (iii) partnership model feasibility (points earn/redeem, referral, co-branded card), (iv) partner&#x27;s technology capability for integration; (b) evaluate ~10–15 potential partners per quarter; (c) shortlist 2–3 for negotiation
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Partnership Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task7" name="Partnership agreement negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partnership agreement negotiation: (a) negotiate terms: (i) points earn rate (e.g., 1 BuildRight point per PHP 50 spent at partner), (ii) points redemption rate (e.g., 100 BuildRight points = PHP 10 discount at partner), (iii) customer data sharing scope per RA 10173 — minimal data exchange (loyalty ID, points balance, transaction amount only), (iv) marketing co-promotion commitments, (v) revenue sharing on cross-referral sales; (b) Legal reviews partnership agreement per W62: data privacy provisions, liability, IP usage, exclusivity, termination; (c) Finance evaluates financial impact: projected points liability increase, partner fees, incremental revenue from partner referrals
Responsible (R): Partnership Manager / Legal / Finance
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task8" name="Technical integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Technical integration: (a) IT integrates partner systems with BuildRight loyalty engine: (i) API for real-time points earn/redeem at partner point-of-sale, (ii) batch file exchange for nightly reconciliation, (iii) loyalty member authentication (phone number or loyalty ID); (b) partner integration tested in UAT: points earn at partner POS, points redeem at partner, statement accuracy; (c) for bank/credit card partners: PCI-DSS compliance verification per W647 data security
Responsible (R): IT / Partner IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task9" name="Launch &amp; co-marketing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Launch &amp; co-marketing: (a) launch partnership with co-marketing campaign per W676: email blast to loyalty members, in-store signage, social media, partner&#x27;s marketing channels; (b) train store staff on partner offer: &quot;Use your BuildRight loyalty card at [Partner] to earn bonus points&quot;; (c) update loyalty program FAQ and app per W615 with partner information and earn/redeem options
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Marketing
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task10" name="Monthly operational monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly operational monitoring: (a) reconcile points earned/redeemed at partner monthly — resolve discrepancies within 5 business days; (b) monitor integration uptime: target 99.5% API availability; (c) track customer engagement: partner transactions per month, unique members engaging, average points earned; (d) Finance processes partner settlement: net points liability transfer or cash settlement per agreement terms
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1186_Task11" name="Quarterly partner performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly partner performance review: (a) measure partnership ROI: (i) incremental BuildRight sales from partner referrals, (ii) incremental loyalty program engagement (active member rate), (iii) points liability cost vs. partnership revenue, (iv) customer satisfaction with partner offers; (b) compare to partnership targets; (c) recommend renewal, renegotiation, or termination per performance; (d) annual contract renewal or termination per W62 agreement terms
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Partnership Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1186_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1186_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1186_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1186_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: partnership agreement and integration review per W62 before build
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
