    <bpmn:process id="W_W1217" name="W1217. Loyalty Program Tier Annual Review, Downgrade Notification &amp; Win-Back Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual tier review date (January 1); system evaluates all 600,000 loyalty members&#x27; trailing 12-month spend against tier qualification thresholds
Frequency: Annual tier evaluation (January); monthly win-back campaigns for downgraded members (February–April)
Volume: ~600,000 members evaluated annually; estimated 15–20% change tier (upgrade + downgrade); ~40,000–60,000 downgraded members requiring win-back outreach
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager
Participants: Loyalty Program Manager, CX Manager, Marketing Coordinator, BI Analyst, Customer Service Rep
Source: workflow W1217 — Loyalty Program Tier Annual Review, Downgrade Notification &amp; Win-Back Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1217_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1217_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1217_Lane2" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1217_Lane3" name="Loyalty Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1217_Lane4" name="Marketing Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1217_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1217_Start6" name="Annual tier review date (January 1); system evaluates all 600,000 loyalty members&#x27;…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1217_Task7" name="Annual tier evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual tier evaluation (January 1): system calculates trailing 12-month spend (January–December) for each member: (a) total spend across all channels (in-store, ecommerce, marketplace), (b) qualify for tier based on thresholds: Bronze (enrolled, no minimum), Silver (≥ PHP 50,000/year), Gold (≥ PHP 150,000/year), Platinum (≥ PHP 500,000/year), (c) system assigns new tier effective January 1; (d) system flags members changing tier: upgraders and downgraders
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (overnight batch)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1217_Task8" name="tier migration report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BI Analyst generates tier migration report: (a) count of members by tier (before and after), (b) upgrade count by tier, (c) downgrade count by tier, (d) churn analysis: members who spent zero in trailing 12 months (fully lapsed), (e) revenue impact: projected change in tier benefit costs (free delivery, exclusive discounts), (f) compare to prior year migration for trend analysis
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Loyalty Program Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1217_Task9" name="Upgrade communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Upgrade communication (January 2–7): system sends automated upgrade notifications via SMS, email, and in-app notification: (a) congratulations message, (b) new tier benefits summary, (c) welcome package per W822 (physical welcome kit for Gold/Platinum), (d) exclusive early access to January sale event as upgrade perk
Responsible (R): System / Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1217_Task10" name="Downgrade communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Downgrade communication (January 7–10): Loyalty Program Manager reviews downgrade list and approves segmented messaging: (a) Soft downgrade (one tier drop, e.g., Gold → Silver): empathetic notification — &quot;You&#x27;re now a valued Silver member&quot; with: (i) Silver tier benefits highlighted, (ii) how much spend needed to regain prior tier, (iii) special &quot;come back&quot; offer: double points for next 30 days; (b) Hard downgrade (multiple tier drop or to Bronze): personal email from Loyalty Program Manager — acknowledge their past loyalty, express desire to continue relationship, offer personalized incentive (e.g., 15% off next purchase); (c) Platinum downgrade (high-value loss): Loyalty Program Manager calls top 100 downgraded Platinum members personally to understand reason and offer retention incentive
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / System
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1217_Task11" name="Win-back campaign">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Win-back campaign (February–April): Marketing Coordinator executes 90-day win-back campaign for downgraded members: (a) Week 1–4: send category-specific offers based on member&#x27;s purchase history (e.g., member who bought tiles last year receives bathroom renovation offer), (b) Week 5–8: escalate incentive — higher discount or bonus points offer, (c) Week 9–12: final outreach — &quot;We miss you&quot; email with exclusive one-time offer; if no response: member moves to low-engagement segment for standard communications
Responsible (R): Marketing Coordinator
Accountable (A): Loyalty Program Manager
Duration: 3 months (ongoing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1217_Task12" name="Tier retention analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Tier retention analysis (April): BI Analyst evaluates win-back campaign effectiveness: (a) what % of downgraded members made a purchase within 90 days?, (b) what incentive level was most effective?, (c) what is the predicted lifetime value of recovered vs. lost members?, (d) recommend tier threshold adjustments if excessive downgrade rates suggest thresholds are too aggressive
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1217_Task13" name="Tier threshold review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Tier threshold review (Q2): Loyalty Program Manager reviews tier qualification thresholds: (a) are thresholds calibrated to member distribution? (e.g., if only 0.5% qualify for Platinum, threshold may be too high), (b) compare spend distribution to threshold levels, (c) benchmark against Philippine retail loyalty programs, (d) propose threshold adjustments to VP Marketing if needed — effective next January
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1217_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1217_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1217_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1217_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Loyalty Program Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1217_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1217_Annotation15" targetRef="W1217_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
