    <bpmn:process id="W_W1274" name="W1274. Customer Loyalty Points Financial Liability Monthly Valuation &amp; Accounting Reserve" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly accounting close cycle (aligned with W9A financial close)
Frequency: Monthly valuation; quarterly deep-dive with actuarial review
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members with outstanding points; estimated PHP 150–250M in outstanding points liability (one register with W1316)
Owner: Finance Analyst (Loyalty Program Accounting)
Participants: Finance Analyst, Controller, Marketing Manager, Loyalty Program Manager
Source: workflow W1274 — Customer Loyalty Points Financial Liability Monthly Valuation &amp; Accounting Reserve</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1274_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1274_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1274_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1274_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1274_Start4" name="Monthly accounting close cycle (aligned with W9A financial close)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1274_Task5" name="Monthly points activity summary">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly points activity summary: system generates monthly points activity report: (a) Points issued this month: total points earned from customer purchases, broken down by channel (POS, ecommerce, B2B), (b) Points redeemed this month: total points used as payment tender per W550, (c) Points expired this month: total points that reached 24-month inactivity and expired per W570, (d) Points balance at month-end: total outstanding unredeemed points across all members, (e) Net points change: issued − redeemed − expired = net new liability
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (report generated T+2)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task6" name="Points liability calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Points liability calculation: Finance Analyst calculates month-end points liability: (a) Gross liability: outstanding points balance × PHP 1.00 redemption value = gross liability, (b) Expected redemption rate: apply historical redemption rate (tracked monthly; current estimate based on trailing 12-month redemption behavior), (c) Adjusted liability: gross liability × expected redemption rate = estimated points that will be redeemed, (d) Deferred revenue allocation: cost of rewards to be redeemed (points redeemed typically result in margin reduction, not pure cash outflow) — calculate expected COGS impact of future redemptions based on average margin of items typically purchased with points, (e) Breakage estimate: points that will never be redeemed (expire or forgotten) — recognized as revenue reduction reversal over the points life
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task7" name="Journal entry posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Journal entry posting: Finance Analyst posts monthly journal entries: (a) Points issuance (at sale): debit — loyalty program expense (COGS basis for expected redemption), credit — deferred revenue — loyalty points liability, (b) Points redemption: debit — deferred revenue — loyalty points liability, credit — revenue (reduction) or COGS adjustment (margin impact), (c) Points expiry (breakage): debit — deferred revenue — loyalty points liability, credit — loyalty program expense (reversal of previously recognized cost), (d) Liability revaluation adjustment: if expected redemption rate changes from prior month, adjust liability to reflect updated estimate
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task8" name="Balance sheet reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Balance sheet reconciliation: Finance Analyst reconciles loyalty points liability account: (a) beginning balance + points issued − points redeemed − points expired + revaluation adjustment = ending balance, (b) ending balance matches system points outstanding × redemption rate, (c) reconcile to general ledger — ensure no orphaned entries or timing differences between system and GL
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task9" name="Redemption rate trend analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Redemption rate trend analysis: Finance Analyst tracks monthly redemption metrics: (a) redemption rate trend (target: 45–55% of issued points redeemed within 12 months), (b) average time to redemption (from issuance to first redemption), (c) redemption by tier — Bronze/Silver/Gold/Platinum members have different redemption behaviors, (d) points outstanding aging: &lt; 6 months, 6–12 months, 12–18 months, 18–24 months (approaching expiry), &gt; 24 months (should have expired), (e) identify if liability is growing faster than revenue (program cost increasing)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task10" name="Quarterly deep-dive and actuarial review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly deep-dive and actuarial review: every quarter (aligned with W1 quarterly cycle): (a) Finance Analyst engages Controller to review redemption rate assumptions, (b) validate breakage estimate against actual expiry data (W570), (c) assess program cost as % of revenue: loyalty program expense ÷ total revenue (target: &lt; 1.5% of revenue), (d) review tier migration impact on liability — Gold/Platinum members earn and redeem at higher rates, (e) assess PFRS 15 disclosure completeness: loyalty program description, liability amount, significant judgments and estimates, (f) if redemption rate changes by &gt; 5% quarter-over-quarter: investigate root cause and adjust forward assumptions
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1274_Task11" name="External audit support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: External audit support: during annual external audit (per W21 internal audit and external auditors): (a) provide auditors with points liability calculation methodology and assumptions, (b) provide system-generated points activity reports for audit testing, (c) support auditors in testing redemption rate assumptions against actual data, (d) respond to audit queries on PFRS 15 compliance
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: ~8 hours/year (during audit)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1274_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1274_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1274_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1274_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Finance Analyst (Loyalty Program Accounting) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Finance Analyst (Loyalty Program Accounting)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1274_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1274_Annotation13" targetRef="W1274_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1274_Flow15" sourceRef="W1274_Start4" targetRef="W1274_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1274_Flow16" sourceRef="W1274_Task5" targetRef="W1274_Task6" />
