    <bpmn:process id="W_W1316" name="W1316. Loyalty Points Liability Accounting, Redemption Forecasting &amp; Program Financial Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly loyalty points liability calculation; or quarter-end deferred revenue posting; or program tier change audit
Frequency: Monthly liability calculation; quarterly financial reporting; annual program audit
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members; ~PHP 62.3B annual revenue with points earned on 55% of transactions (B2C + ecommerce); estimated outstanding points liability: PHP 150–250M at any time
Owner: Finance Controller
Participants: Finance Controller, Finance Analyst, Loyalty Program Manager, VP Marketing, External Auditor
Source: workflow W1316 — Loyalty Points Liability Accounting, Redemption Forecasting &amp; Program Financial Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1316_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1316_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1316_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1316_Lane3" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1316_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1316_Start5" name="Monthly loyalty points liability calculation; or quarter-end deferred revenue posting; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1316_Task6" name="Monthly points liability calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly points liability calculation: (a) system calculates loyalty points liability at month-end: (i) total outstanding points balance: points earned and not yet redeemed across all 600,000 members, (ii) redemption value: outstanding points × PHP 1.00/point = gross liability, (iii) breakage adjustment: apply estimated breakage rate (% of points historically never redeemed — BuildRight estimates 15–20% breakage based on program history); (iv) net liability = gross liability × (1 – breakage rate); (v) compare to prior month: is the liability increasing (more points earned than redeemed) or decreasing (high redemption activity)?; (b) Finance Analyst reviews calculation: (i) verify points earning data matches POS transaction records, (ii) verify points redemption data matches loyalty engine records, (iii) check for anomalies: sudden spike in points earning (promotion-driven earning) or redemption (quarterly member engagement campaigns)
Responsible (R): System / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1316_Task7" name="Quarterly deferred revenue posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly deferred revenue posting: (a) at quarter-end, Finance Controller posts loyalty points deferred revenue entries: (i) calculate points earned during the quarter × estimated redemption rate (80–85%) × stand-alone selling price (PHP 1.00/point) = deferred revenue to recognize, (ii) allocate transaction price per PFRS 15: total POS revenue allocated between (a) goods delivered (recognized immediately) and (b) loyalty points (deferred), (iii) journal entry: debit Revenue (reduction), credit Deferred Revenue — Loyalty Points (liability), (iv) for points redeemed during the quarter: debit Deferred Revenue — Loyalty Points, credit Revenue (recognition); (b) Finance Controller reviews and approves entries; (c) entries included in quarterly consolidated financial statements per W17
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1316_Task8" name="Breakage rate estimation &amp; annual update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Breakage rate estimation &amp; annual update: (a) annual, Finance Analyst performs detailed breakage analysis: (i) historical redemption pattern by cohort (members who joined in year X: what % of their total earned points have been redeemed after 1 year, 2 years, 3 years?), (ii) points expiration analysis (if BuildRight&#x27;s program has expiration — points expire after 2 years of inactivity), (iii) tier-based redemption rates (Platinum members redeem more frequently than Bronze — tier-weighted breakage rate is more accurate), (iv) update the breakage assumption used in liability calculation per PFRS 15 requirement for current estimates; (b) Finance Controller approves updated breakage rate; (c) if breakage rate changes significantly: adjust quarterly deferred revenue postings retroactively per PFRS 15 cumulative catch-up adjustment
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 8–16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1316_Task9" name="Redemption forecasting &amp; cash flow impact">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Redemption forecasting &amp; cash flow impact: (a) quarterly, Loyalty Program Manager and Finance Analyst forecast redemption volumes: (i) historical redemption trends (seasonal: higher redemption during ber-months and back-to-school), (ii) upcoming program promotions (double points weekends generate earning spikes that translate to redemption spikes 2–3 months later), (iii) planned redemption campaigns (member-only sales where points can be used for partial payment), (iv) tier upgrade waves (when members upgrade tier, redemption activity typically increases as members engage more); (b) Finance Analyst estimates cash flow impact: (i) redemption at checkout (points used as payment) reduces cash collection at POS — estimated PHP 15–25M/month in points-as-payment, (ii) redemption for rewards (merchandise, gift items) creates COGS without corresponding revenue — estimated PHP 3–5M/month (combined redemption ≤ the ~274–292M points/yr net-redeemable canon), (iii) net cash flow impact of loyalty program on monthly working capital; (c) forecast shared with Treasury for cash flow planning per W34
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1316_Task10" name="Annual loyalty program financial audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual loyalty program financial audit: (a) during annual external audit, auditor reviews loyalty program accounting: (i) points liability calculation methodology and assumptions, (ii) breakage rate estimation and supporting data, (iii) deferred revenue journal entries and PFRS 15 compliance, (iv) loyalty program terms and conditions (are there any changes that affect the liability?), (v) points system integrity (do points earned + opening balance - redeemed + expired = closing balance?); (b) Finance Analyst prepares audit workpapers: program terms, liability calculation, breakage analysis, deferred revenue entries, reconciliation of points balances; (c) address any auditor findings or adjustments
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–8 hours during annual audit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1316_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1316_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1316_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
