    <bpmn:process id="W_W1434" name="W1434. Loyalty Program Partner Quarterly Rebate Settlement, Tier Benefit Cost Allocation &amp; ROI Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly loyalty program partner settlement cycle; or annual loyalty program ROI review; or new partner onboarding
Frequency: Quarterly rebate settlement; annual ROI analysis and partner review
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members; ~15–20 loyalty program partners (banks, insurance, fuel, home service providers); quarterly partner transactions: ~270,000–360,000+ partner earn/redeem events per quarter (per W1186&#x27;s monthly engagement register)
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager
Participants: Loyalty Program Manager, Finance Analyst, Partner Account Manager, CMO, Controller
Source: workflow W1434 — Loyalty Program Partner Quarterly Rebate Settlement, Tier Benefit Cost Allocation &amp; ROI Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1434_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1434_Lane1" name="Loyalty Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1434_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1434_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1434_Start4" name="Quarterly loyalty program partner settlement cycle; or annual loyalty program ROI review…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1434_Task5" name="Quarterly partner transaction reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly partner transaction reconciliation: (a) Loyalty Program Manager reconciles partner transactions for the quarter: (i) total points earned at partner locations by BuildRight members (BuildRight owes partner for these points — typically PHP 0.50–1.00 per point earned), (ii) total points redeemed at BuildRight by partner program members (partner owes BuildRight — typically PHP 0.80–1.20 per point redeemed), (iii) net settlement = (points earned at partner × BuildRight cost/point) − (points redeemed at BuildRight × partner reimbursement/point), (b) verify transaction counts against partner reporting: resolve discrepancies (missing transactions, incorrect point values, system integration errors)
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1434_Task6" name="Quarterly rebate settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly rebate settlement: (a) for each partner: (i) compute net payable/receivable: if net settlement is positive (BuildRight owes partner), generate AP voucher per W7; if negative (partner owes BuildRight), generate AR invoice per W16, (ii) Controller approves settlement amounts, (iii) settle via bank transfer per W34, (b) for tier benefit costs: (i) compute cost of tier benefits provided during quarter: free delivery events (Gold/Platinum), exclusive discount value, partner service vouchers, (ii) allocate costs: BuildRight share vs. partner share per agreement, (iii) recover partner share via quarterly settlement
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1434_Task7" name="Partner performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Partner performance review: (a) Loyalty Program Manager reviews each partner&#x27;s quarterly performance: (i) transaction volume: are members actively using the partner benefit? (ii) member acquisition: how many new loyalty members joined via partner channel? (iii) revenue impact: estimated incremental BuildRight revenue from partner-referred members, (iv) cost per acquisition: partner settlement costs ÷ new members acquired via partner, (b) identify underperforming partners: low transaction volume, high settlement cost with low incremental revenue → candidates for renegotiation or termination
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1434_Task8" name="Annual loyalty program ROI analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual loyalty program ROI analysis: (a) Finance Analyst prepares annual loyalty program ROI: (i) total program costs: (A) points liability increase (W1274), (B) partner settlements, (C) tier benefit costs (delivery, discounts, services), (D) program operations (staff, technology, marketing), (ii) total program revenue impact: (E) incremental revenue from loyalty members vs. non-members (loyalty members have ~20% higher ATV and ~15% higher visit frequency per industry benchmarks), (F) reduced churn value (retained members × annual revenue per member), (G) partner referral revenue, (iii) ROI = (E + F + G − A − B − C − D) ÷ (A + B + C + D), (b) CMO presents ROI to CEO/CFO: is the loyalty program generating positive returns? should tier structure be adjusted? should partner portfolio be expanded or reduced?
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): CMO / CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1434_Task9" name="Partner agreement renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Partner agreement renewal: (a) annually, Loyalty Program Manager reviews partner agreements expiring: (i) negotiate renewal terms based on performance data from Step 3, (ii) for high-performing partners: explore expanded benefits (higher earn rates, exclusive offers), (iii) for underperforming partners: renegotiate terms or allow agreement to lapse, (iv) Controller reviews financial terms for arm&#x27;s-length compliance (related-party implications if any partner is affiliated with BuildRight ownership), (b) new partner recruitment: identify gaps in partner portfolio (e.g., no home insurance partner, no appliance brand partner) and recruit per W674 (loyalty partner management)
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / Controller
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1434_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1434_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1434_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1434_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Loyalty Program Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Loyalty Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
