    <bpmn:process id="W_W1499" name="W1499. Customer Loyalty Program Tier Qualification Period Reset, Points Expiration Management &amp; Downgrade Communication" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual tier qualification period ends (calendar year); also monthly points expiration sweep for points older than 24 months
Frequency: Annual tier reset (January); monthly points expiration sweep; quarterly downgrade prevention campaign
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty program members; ~30% qualify for Silver or higher tier; ~7–10% of members downgraded each year (~40,000–60,000, per W1217); ~5–10% of outstanding points expire annually
Owner: Loyalty Program Coordinator
Participants: Loyalty Program Coordinator, Marketing Associate, Customer Service Representative, BI Analyst
Source: workflow W1499 — Customer Loyalty Program Tier Qualification Period Reset, Points Expiration Management &amp; Downgrade Communication</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1499_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1499_Lane1" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1499_Lane2" name="Loyalty Program Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1499_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1499_Lane4" name="Marketing Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1499_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1499_Start6" name="Annual tier qualification period ends (calendar year); also monthly points expiration…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1499_Task7" name="Annual tier recalculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual tier recalculation (December): (a) BI Analyst runs year-to-date spend aggregation for all loyalty members; (b) system compares each member&#x27;s 12-month spend to tier thresholds; (c) members who achieved a higher tier: upgraded effective January 1; (d) members who fall below their current tier threshold: flagged for downgrade review; (e) edge cases reviewed: members within 10% of threshold (e.g., Silver member at PHP 47,000 spend — should they be &quot;rounded up&quot;?); (f) final tier assignments approved by Loyalty Program Coordinator with VP Merchandising sign-off for any exception overrides
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Loyalty Program Coordinator
Duration: 2–3 days in December</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1499_Task8" name="Downgrade prevention campaign">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Downgrade prevention campaign (November): Before tier reset: (a) Loyalty Program Coordinator identifies members at risk of downgrade: (i) currently Silver/Gold/Platinum but projected to fall below threshold based on year-to-date spend and typical December purchasing pattern; (ii) count by tier: ~25,000–45,000 Silver at risk, ~10,000–15,000 Gold at risk, ~2,500–4,000 Platinum at risk (consistent with the ~40,000–60,000 annual downgrades); (b) targeted retention campaign launched: (i) Silver at risk: &quot;You&#x27;re PHP X away from keeping Silver — shop now to maintain your benefits&quot;; personalized SMS/email with amount needed; (ii) Gold at risk: same messaging + exclusive December in-store event invitation; (iii) Platinum at risk: personal call from Loyalty Program Coordinator offering one-time tier extension for members within 15% of threshold (discretionary override); (c) campaign runs November 15 – December 31; daily monitoring of qualifying purchases
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Coordinator / Marketing Associate
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1499_Task9" name="Tier downgrade communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Tier downgrade communication (January): For members who do downgrade: (a) personalized email sent January 2 explaining: (i) new tier effective immediately; (ii) specific benefits lost; (iii) how to requalify in the current year; (iv) any grace period benefits (e.g., Silver benefits extended through January as courtesy); (b) SMS notification for members without email on file; (c) for Platinum-to-Gold downgrades: personal call from Loyalty Program Coordinator acknowledging the change and reiterating value of continued membership; (d) all downgrade communications reviewed by Marketing Associate for tone sensitivity
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Coordinator / Marketing Associate
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1499_Task10" name="Monthly points expiration sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly points expiration sweep: Monthly: (a) system identifies points earned &gt; 24 months ago that have not been redeemed; (b) 60-day warning: members with points expiring in 60 days receive email/SMS: &quot;Your PHP X worth of points expire on [date] — redeem now!&quot;; (c) 30-day warning: final reminder with specific redemption suggestions (product recommendations based on purchase history); (d) on expiration date: unredeemed points zeroed out; (e) expiration value tracked for program liability accounting (points liability reduction = PHP value of expired points); (f) monthly expiration report: total points expired, number of members affected, average value per member
Responsible (R): System / Loyalty Program Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO (for liability impact)
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1499_Task11" name="Points expiration redemption campaign">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Points expiration redemption campaign: For members in the 60-day warning window: (a) Marketing Associate creates targeted promotions: (i) &quot;Double Points Weekend&quot; for purchases that earn points (not relevant for expiring points but drives engagement); (ii) curated &quot;Redeem Your Points&quot; product selections in the loyalty app; (iii) limited-time bonus: &quot;Redeem expiring points for 1.5x value on select items this weekend&quot;; (b) campaign effectiveness tracked: redemption rate for expiring-point members vs. general member base; (c) Loyalty Program Coordinator adjusts campaign tactics based on monthly results
Responsible (R): Marketing Associate / Loyalty Program Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1499_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1499_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1499_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1499_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-279 (ensure controlled execution — Loyalty Program Operations (PA-13.2).) | - operational: Loyalty Program Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Loyalty Program Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1499_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1499_Annotation13" targetRef="W1499_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow15" sourceRef="W1499_Start6" targetRef="W1499_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow16" sourceRef="W1499_Task7" targetRef="W1499_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow17" sourceRef="W1499_Task8" targetRef="W1499_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow18" sourceRef="W1499_Task9" targetRef="W1499_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow19" sourceRef="W1499_Task10" targetRef="W1499_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1499_Flow20" sourceRef="W1499_Task11" targetRef="W1499_End12" />
